meta {
  name: GET vehicle-information battery-health (State of Health)
  type: http
  seq: 56
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/vehicle-information/{{vin}}/battery-health
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  v4.7.12 — Škoda HV battery State-of-Health read.
  Source: MyŠkoda 8.16.0 (versionCode 260821007), new Retrofit route on
  VehicleInformationApi (same host + Bearer as /renders and /equipment).
  App-side gated on the capability id BATTERY_HEALTH_STATE.

  Response shape (BatteryHealthStatusDto):
    {
      "status": "HEALTHY" | "NEEDS_MAINTENANCE" | "UNAVAILABLE",
      "remainingCapacity": 96,          // int, may be null
      "carCapturedTimestamp": "2026-09-16T10:12:00Z"
    }

  Use case: battery_soh_pct (0..100) + health_status attribute on the
  existing SoH sensor. 403/404 memoised per VIN for the client lifetime.

  Implementation: SkodaClient.get_battery_health() in cariad/api/skoda.py,
  consumed in get_status() next to the software-update read.
}
